# Security Guidelines

## Mandatory controls
- Authentication (JWT / session as implemented in `apps/api` auth module)
- Authorization on every protected route and use case
- Encryption in transit (HTTPS / WSS in production)
- Encryption at rest for sensitive data stores

## Secrets — never commit
- Passwords, tokens, API keys, `.env`, credentials JSON
- Use `.env.example` for documented keys only

## Logging
- Never log secrets, full tokens, or passwords

## Validation
- Validate all external input (DTOs, query params, WebSocket payloads)
- Mobile: sanitize user content length and types before API calls

## Mobile
- Production API URLs via `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` env — not hardcoded LAN IPs in release builds

## Docker / deploy
- Non-root user, health checks, minimal exposed ports (see `apps/api/Dockerfile`)
